From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:19:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/49] R7: the direct tree decoder skips strconv.Unquote only
 for names it returns unchanged

LoadTree and LoadTreeNodeReader unquoted a node name only when it contained
a backslash. A name with a raw double quote or a raw newline (a tree written
by another tool) was accepted where stock fails with "Unquote: invalid
syntax", in check, ls and restore.

The call is now skipped only when the name has no backslash, no double
quote, no byte below 0x20 and is valid UTF-8, which are the names
strconv.Unquote returns as they are. Every other name goes through stock's
call, so the same trees are rejected with the same error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
